2) Global Systems
2.1 City Stability (−3..+3)

−3 Panic: riots, +25% mugging, clinics overwhelmed, curfews by whoever pays the guards.

−2 Unrest: crowd surges can steal a grid action; Black Market bolder.

−1 Brittle: pickpockets frequent; Matriarchy patrols thin.

0 Steady: baseline.

+1 Calm: fewer street crimes; clinic schedules hold.

+2 Coordinated: volunteer patrols; relief kitchens; rare-cure queue opens.

+3 Proud: festivals; −20% street crime; nobles behave.

2.2 Miner Payout Index (MPI 0..100)

0–25 Crisis: evictions surge; “Desperation-tier” Village quests; Black Market crystal stock +2 tiers.

26–50 Squeezed: protests, heavier Merchant presence; clinic drug prices creep.

51–75 Fair: citizen thefts dip.

76–100 Flourishing: Thieves flip to “Robin Hood” mode (merchant raids > citizen muggings).

Economic levers:
Every −10 MPI → +5% theft in Stone Village, Black Market crystal +1 tier.
Every +10 MPI → clinic rare-cure stock improves; Black Market crystal −1 tier.

2.3 Cult Pressure (0..100)

0–25 Low: sermons are noise.

26–60 Rising: street “Speed Fervor” rushes may steal a player action in public scenes.

61–100 High: “blessing booths” apply micro-curses; palace access gets blocked by bribes.

2.4 Reputation couplers

High Cult soft-caps Matriarchy rep ceiling until Orion is exposed.

High Underground triggers friction with both civics unless laundered via “community jobs” or official contracts.

3) Districts and Access
3.1 Entry rules (centralize in canEnter(districtId))

Noble District: attire check or 100-credit deposit; fail → escorted out, etiquette flagged 24h.

Queen’s Circle: pass.queen_intro or rep.matriarchy ≥ 100 or pass.forged_circle.

Black Market: discover Whispering Alley rune + entrance fee scaled to visible wealth, or Orlen vouches after “Seized Home.”

3.2 District briefs

Noble: Emerald Spire Bathhouse, Gilded Library, Silk Bazaar. Private clinics mint “legal impunity” receipts.

Queen’s Circle: palace, duchess halls, Healing Hand Clinic, Grand Archives.
Shadow companion: ally.thal=1 → stealth routes, 1 emergency extract/day, +10% guard-path success.

Grand Stone Weight Station: Great Scales, assay offices. Bug the scales to expose tare scheme.

Stone Village: families, seized homes, rumor hub (Eris), recruitable Orlen. Events shift with MPI.

Market (day)/Black Market (night): Iron Will Smithy, Desert Sundries. Deyla’s Den: neutral-predatory auctions; fees drop with Merchant rep; stock quality rises with Underground rep.

Outskirts & Gauntlet Entry: city edge to Lich Gauntlet; named roamers at night can “visit.”

4) Factions

Matriarchy (civic): clinics, passes, adjudication. Failure: Queen dies/displaced; Stability tanks; rare cures rationed.

Merchant Guild (economic): judges, scales, warehousing, supply gating. Failure: exposés stick; MPI rises; nobles stop cover.

Underground (private): routes, secrets, deniable force. Failure: internal cannibalism; Deyla blacklist; counter-contracts.

Cult of Orion (public pseudo-religious): crowds, cursed “blessings,” fear leverage. Failure: debate loss + record leaks; harassment collapses.

Deyla alignment fix: neutral-predatory. Not Guild. Guild rep reduces auction fees; Underground rep unlocks stock tiers.

5) Key NPCs (motivation • leverage • secrets • breakpoints)

Queen Aramia: protect social compact • legitimacy, clinics • poison vector hides in noble supply • miss 2 windows → escalates; cure needs ledger + antidote.

Duchess Mira: break Guild; build co-ops • miners, procurement • quiet legal team • deliver proof → unlock “Seizure Writs.”

Duchess Selinne: stability first • nobles, backchannels • blackmail-prone • can become regent or be hardened.

Lady Velira: stop reforms • salons, private guards • bathhouse hub; poisoning ring • core antagonist in Illness arc.

Royal Physician Jorren: survival/penance • sickroom access • falsified charts • redeem for clinic buffs or expose.

Captain Thal: protect Queen • keys/routes/loyal guards • dead-drops • ally.thal=1 gives mechanical routes without party bloat.

Master Deyla: margins > morality • auctions, contracts • duplicated “insurance” ledger • hand ledger to Matriarchy → Seizure Writs once; to Merchants → −15% Black Market fees 48h.

Orion Ophemium: influence via fear • crowds, curses • staged miracles bought from Deyla • public debate pivot.

Eris (Tavern): community survival • rumor mesh • eviction list + judge name.

Foreman Calder: dignity for labor • strike leverage • tunnel bypass for assay; ties thieves.

Orlen (Exiled Miner): claw back life • local muscle • becomes thief lieutenant or bandit captain.